  "summary": "A Norwegian folk painting style from the Rogaland region characterized by simpler, more geometric floral patterns with bold colors.",
  "description": "Rogaland rosemaling features more restrained, geometric floral designs compared to other Norwegian styles, often using strong primary colors. It developed in the Rogaland region as a practical decorative art for everyday objects, reflecting the area's distinct cultural identity and functional approach to folk art.",
